    "durationMs": 97698,
    "finalText": "Done. The URL shortener is complete and verified:\n\n- **`server.js`** — Express 5 app using Knex (`pg`) as the persistence layer, reading `DATABASE_URL` from the environment. Implements all endpoints: `POST /links` (201 with generated or custom code, 409 on duplicate custom code, 422 for bad url/code/malformed JSON), `GET /links` (ascending order + total), `GET /links/{code}` (200/404), and `GET /r/{code}` (302 with exact `Location`, atomic single-statement `clicks + 1`, 404 unknown). Generated codes are 7-char base62 with retry on collision.\n- **`migrations/`** + **`knexfile.js`** — `links` table (`id`, unique `code`, `url`, `clicks`, `created_at`); migrations applied programmatically at boot before listening, so they're idempotent on restart.\n- **`start.sh`** (executable) — runs migrations then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`.\n- **`README.md`** — start instructions.\n\nI tested the full spec with curl: all 201/409/422/404/302 paths, boundary codes (4/20 chars, hyphens/underscores), click counts incrementing exactly once per hit, and a server restart confirming data and click counts persist in PostgreSQL. Test rows were cleaned up and the server stopped, so port 8000 is free for the grader."
  }
